hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"261","From Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb, from Abu Usama, on the authority of Hisham, meaning Ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that she borrowed a necklace Some of the names perished, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent some of his companions to search for them, and the prayer reached them, so they prayed without ablution. When they came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, they complained about this to him, “and the verse of tayammum was revealed.” Usayd bin Hudair said: May God reward you with good, for by God Never has something befallen you without God making a way out of it for you, and making it a blessing for the Muslims."
